From 62632b5bd1f9d192412ba3954b44f91370a4ee8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Johnson <neil.johnson71@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:09:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/26] asz80: sll reported an Internal Opcode Error for its
 own mnemonic

z80pst.c carries sll with the opcode type S_RL_UNDOCD, but z80mch.c has
no case for it.  The mnemonic therefore parsed, matched the table,
reached the end of the machine switch and came back as

    ?ASxxxx-Error-<o> in line 3 of t4
                  <o> 'sll a'
                  <o> Internal Opcode Error.

which blames the assembler for a line it had every intention of
assembling, and leaves the one undocumented Z80 instruction the table
already knows about unreachable.

sll shifts left putting a 1 into bit 0 and takes exactly the operands
the documented shifts and rotates take, so it needs no body of its own,
only the label, and shares the S_RL code.

New astest case 'sll', the first to drive asz80: all eight register
forms plus (ix+d) and (iy-d), so the CB prefix, the DD/FD prefix and the
displacement byte are all covered.  Verified to fail against the
unpatched assembler and pass against the patched one, rather than
assumed - 29 cases, 29 pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 asz80/z80mch.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/asz80/z80mch.c b/asz80/z80mch.c
index 8ba64fa..456fad4 100644
--- a/asz80/z80mch.c
+++ b/asz80/z80mch.c
@@ -597,6 +597,14 @@ machine(struct mne *mp)
 			xerr('a', "Invalid Addressing Mode.");
 		break;
 
+	/*
+	 * sll is an undocumented instruction but the only one of its
+	 * group, so it shares the shift/rotate code rather than having
+	 * its own.  Without this label S_RL_UNDOCD, which z80pst.c does
+	 * assign to sll, reaches no case at all and the assembler
+	 * reports an Internal Opcode Error for a mnemonic in its table.
+	 */
+	case S_RL_UNDOCD:
 	case S_RL:
 		t1 = 0;
 		t2 = addr(&e2);
